 "answerBank": [
  {
   "q": "Do I have to believe any of this?",
   "a": "No — assessments test literacy, never belief. The tier system exists precisely so you can study claims rigorously without affirming them. Read, tier, argue.",
   "ref": "il01-hermetic-foundations"
  },
  {
   "q": "Why study esotericism in a tech academy?",
   "a": "Historiography, primary-source literacy, and the tier discipline transfer everywhere — including to evaluating technical claims. Plus: the history of computing (Dee, cybernetics) runs through this material.",
   "ref": "il01-dee-enochian"
  },
  {
   "q": "Isn't the CCRU just internet mysticism?",
   "a": "The seminar treats it as texts with a documented context (Warwick, 1990s) and a CONTESTED theory (hyperstition). Read the corpus, tier the claims, argue the status — that's the work.",
   "ref": "il01-ccru-seminar"
  },
  {
   "q": "Where do I start reading?",
   "a": "The Asclepius (complete, short), then Dee's biography, then the Land/CCRU corpus in reading order. Commonplace book from day one.",
   "ref": "il01-hermetic-foundations"
  },
  {
   "q": "What's the journal for?",
   "a": "It's the assessment artifact: every reading logged with tier, evidence, and your open question. It demonstrates the method — which is the actual skill being taught.",
   "ref": "il01-dee-enochian"
  },
  {
   "q": "How do TRADITIONAL claims get treated?",
   "a": "Reported accurately, labeled honestly — never endorsed, never mocked. 'The lineage claims X' is a DOCUMENTED fact about the claim, whatever X's own tier is.",
   "ref": "il01-hermetic-foundations"
  }
 ],
